lesson: 215
title: Clean socks for a week
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: A week has 7 days. If you put on a clean pair of socks every day, you need 7 pairs for a week.
explain: A pair is 2 socks, so a week of clean pairs is 7 × 2 = 14 socks for each person.
explain: 3 children going away for a week, a clean pair each day: 3 × 7 = 21 pairs, and 21 × 2 = 42 socks.
vars: a=name c=2..6 z=2..5
answer: c * 7 * 2
exercise: {c} children go to camp for a week. Each child wears a clean pair of socks every day. How many socks do they pack?
exercise: {a}'s family of {c} goes on holiday for one week, and everyone puts on a clean pair of socks each day. How many socks must they pack?
exercise: {c} cousins stay at Grandma's for a week. Each needs a clean pair of socks every day. How many socks does Grandma wash at the end?
exercise: For a week-long trip, {c} scouts each pack a clean pair of socks for every day. How many socks are packed?
exercise: How many socks are worn in a week by {c} people who each put on a fresh pair every day?
exercise: {c} of us away for a week, clean pair each day. how many socks to pack
exercise: camp is a week, there's {c} kids, mum says fresh socks every day. socks total?
exercise: {a} packs for the week for all {c+1} of us — no wait, {c}, dad's not coming. clean pair a day each. how many socks
exercise: {a} reckons {c} kids need {c*7} socks for a week. that's pairs not socks innit. how many socks
exercise: week at the beach, {c} people, {z} towels each lol but clean pair of socks a day. how many socks
exercise: {c} kids, 1 week, new pair every day. socks?
test: Every day for a week, each of {c} children pulls on a pair of clean socks. Find the number of socks that end up in the wash.
test: A clean pair of socks a day is the rule for the {c} people on a seven-day boat trip. How many socks do they take?
test: How many single socks do {c} campers need if each wants a fresh pair every day of the week?
test: {c} of us, a week away, fresh socks daily. how many socks
test: grandma's for a week, {c} of us cousins, she makes us change socks every day. how many socks she washing
test: {c} children go on a week's school trip and take {z} books each. They change into a clean pair of socks every day. How many socks do they pack?
exam: A party of {c} persons undertakes a journey of one week's duration, each person donning a clean pair of socks daily. Determine the aggregate number of socks required.
exam: Given that each of {c.words} children is to be supplied with a fresh pair of socks for every day of a week, ascertain the total number of individual socks.
exam: Compute the number of socks laundered following a week in which {c} residents each wore a single clean pair per day.
exam: It is stipulated that {c} participants in a residential course of seven days' duration shall change their socks daily. State the number of socks to be packed.
exercise: {c+1} cousins were going to camp for a week, but one "came down with something" and stayed at home. Each of the others takes a clean pair of socks for every day. How many socks are packed?
exercise: {a} "misremembered" packing the socks, so none got packed, crap. {c} of us, a week away, clean pair a day. how many socks we gotta buy
test: Mum says the holiday cottage "has a lot of character", which means there is no washing machine, so each of the {c} children needs a clean pair of socks for each of the 7 days. How many socks must they pack?
